# neurorights_swarm_control.sai
# Superintelligence data-fragment
# Scope: Neurorights-aware nanoswarm control interfaces within the nanorobotics stack.

fragment NeurorightsSwarmControlV1 {
  id: "neurorights-swarm-control.v1"
  version: "1.0.0"

  intent: """
  Define the high-level interfaces and invariants for nanoswarm controllers that
  must honor neurorights constraints, per-host nociceptive floors, EcoWealth metrics,
  and distributed sovereignty guard meshes. This fragment does not bind to any
  specific blockchain or L2; it constrains Rust crates and ALN/AKL shards that
  participate in neurorights-aware nanoswarm actuation.
  """

  domains: [
    "nanorobotics.swarm",
    "nanorobotics.guardmesh",
    "nanorobotics.neurorights",
    "nanorobotics.ecoswarm"
  ]

  invariants: [
    "No nanoswarm actuation command may be issued without passing through at least one neurorights-aware guard.",
    "Pain/fear shield LUTs must be monotone non-increasing in output clamp factor with respect to pain and fear indices.",
    "Effective ceilings for host physiology parameters are the min of universal corridors and host-personal ceilings.",
    "Any global Brake command must be approved by a supermajority of configured sovereignty guard nodes, except in explicitly defined emergency-solo paths.",
    "Eco-swarm missions must not violate VampiricHealthcareEnvelope constraints for any host when the host is coupled to the mission."
  ]

  key_objects: [
    "PainFearShieldLut",
    "EcoSwarmMissionPlan",
    "MeshGuardConfig",
    "MeshBrakeProposal",
    "EcoWealthMetrics"
  ]

  rust_crates: [
    "nanorobotics-neuroshield",
    "nanorobotics-ecoswarm",
    "nanorobotics-guardmesh"
  ]

  design_notes: """
  The nanorobotics-neuroshield crate owns the pain/fear LUT generation and
  runtime clamp evaluation. It presents a pure Rust API such that hardware-
  facing components can embed the LUT in firmware or FPGA images.

  The nanorobotics-ecoswarm crate owns mission scheduling that optimizes
  for energy and carbon given region-specific grid carbon catalogs and solar
  profiles. It communicates with higher-level AI-chat layers via data-only
  plan objects and never executes arbitrary code from LLMs.

  The nanorobotics-guardmesh crate owns supermajority-based Brake decisions.
  It does not implement a full consensus protocol; instead, it provides a
  deterministic threshold engine that can be called from higher-level gossip
  or message-passing layers. All identities are bound to DIDs and domain-
  separated signatures.

  This .sai fragment is intentionally language-agnostic. It exists to anchor
  the invariants and the division of responsibilities so that Rust crates and
  ALN shards can be checked against a stable superintelligence specification.
  """
}
